    "body": "## Motivation\n\n#41282 keeps `RotaryEmbedding.cos_sin_cache` fp32 on HIP so the fused QSA indexer kernel can read it, and stopped casting it to the query dtype in `forward_cuda`. On HIP, though, every rope without a fused KV-cache write goes through the `sgl_kernel.rotary_embedding` fallback, and that kernel reads the cache as `scalar_t` of the query. With a bf16/fp16 query it now fails during CUDA graph capture:\n\n```\nFile \".../sglang/srt/layers/rotary_embedding/base.py\", line 455, in forward_cuda\nFile \".../sgl_kernel/elementwise.py\", line 414, in rotary_embedding\nRuntimeError: expected scalar type BFloat16 but found Float\nException: Capture cuda graph failed: expected scalar type BFloat16 but found Float\n```\n\nThis takes down `stage-a-test-1-gpu-small-amd` (Llama in `test_basic_sanity.py` / `test_basic_sanity_eagle3.py`), so every AMD stage B/C lane is skipped. Examples: [run 37180583674](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37180583674/job/111372273784), [run 37187809051](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37187809051/job/111393476849) (`expected scalar type Half but found Float`).\n\n## Modifications\n\n`python/sglang/srt/layers/rotary_embedding/base.py`:\n\n- The HIP fallback branch of `forward_cuda` passes `_cos_sin_cache_as(query.dtype)`: a copy of the fp32 buffer cast to the query dtype. It is cast once and reused until the buffer is replaced (moved or extended by `_ensure_cos_sin_cache_length`). The kernel sees the same values as before #41282.\n- The registered buffer stays fp32, so the QSA indexer and the other HIP consumers #41282 targets are unchanged. The device move now only reassigns when the device actually differs.\n\nCUDA, XPU and the other platforms are untouched.\n\n`test/registered/unit/layers/test_rope_hip_fallback_cache_dtype.py` (CPU): with `_is_hip` patched on, the fallback gets a query-dtype cache equal to the fp32 buffer cast, the copy is reused across calls, the buffer stays fp32, and an extended buffer produces a fresh copy.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Unit test passes on CPU ([`base-a-test-cpu (1)`](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37192390255/job/111407259395))\n- [x] CI: `stage-a-test-1-gpu-small-amd` passes again, 8/8 files including `test_basic_sanity.py` and `test_basic_sanity_eagle3.py`, with no `expected scalar type` error, on ROCm 10 ([run 37192390233](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37192390233/job/111407743965)), ROCm 7.2.4 ([run 37204337317](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37204337317/job/111442354031)) and ROCm 7.2.0 ([run 37204341202](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37204341202/job/111442353472))\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37192390255](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37192390255)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37192399978](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37192399978)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37192390233](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37192390233)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
